  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nAccording to [StructuredSerializeInternal step 22](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/structured-data.html#structuredserializeinternal), any object with internal slots other than `[[Prototype]]` or `[[Extensible]]` that isn't specifically handled should throw a DataCloneError DOMException. I don't know if whatwg internal slots are identical to tc39 internal slots, but according to the [ES spec](https://262.ecma-international.org/#sec-object-internal-methods-and-internal-slots): \"All objects have an internal slot named [[PrivateElements]],...\" and so even plain objects should be rejected if the two specs are talking about the same internal slots, as it appears they intend to be according to [\"This section uses the terminology and typographic conventions from the JavaScript specification.\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/structured-data.html#safe-passing-of-structured-data).\r\n\r\nThat's the one internal slot that I found. There could be others.  (I get that things are this way for pragmatic reasons, but at the very least is seems like `[[PrivateElements]]` should be added, if not some more general waffling about what internal slots might be important or something.)",
